# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Antigravity
# Google's Antigravity CLI (agy) runs as its own ACP server (`agy acp`). Its
# state lives in one folder, ~/.gemini unless --gemini-dir names another, so
# each slot gets a private one (homes/antigravity, homes/antigravity-key)
# passed as --gemini-dir to everything agentctl runs, and HOME stays the
# machine user's for the agent's own shell. AGY_CLI_FORCE_FILE_TOKEN_STORAGE
# keeps the sign-in in that folder: otherwise agy puts it in the login
# keychain whenever that is unlocked, one item shared by every slot and person.
#
# The subscription (a Google account with Gemini: Google AI Pro or Ultra, or
# the free tier) signs in like Claude: `agy acp --login` prints a Google link,
# the person approves it, antigravity.google shows a code, and the code is
# pasted back. It runs in a fresh folder inside the login folder; on success
# the sign-in file moves into homes/antigravity. agy refreshes it itself, so
# its fingerprint is the refresh token's, which a refresh keeps. The account
# is the email in the file, kept in secrets/antigravity.json.
#
# The check and the model listing are one ACP session (`buzz-acp models`): it
# answers -32000 "Authentication required" when signed out and lists the
# models and thinking levels this sign-in offers, calling no model. Each
# listed id is <model>-<level> (gemini-4-neon-xhigh), and agy takes that id to
# set both (session/set_model), so an agent's model and effort go to buzz-acp
# as one BUZZ_ACP_MODEL. A key (GEMINI_API_KEY) works only with modelProvider
# "gemini" in the home's settings.json; agy lists models for any key without
# checking it, so a key is checked with Google's own model list.

AGY = {"login": ["acp", "--login", "--disable-telemetry"], "service": "Google",
       # The sign-in file in the home ({"token": {access_token, refresh_token, ...},
       # "auth_method", "id_token_email"}, as 1.5.18 writes it), and the state that
       # goes with it (which ACP auth method it is, onboarding done).
       "cred": ("antigravity-cli", "antigravity-oauth-token"),
       "with_cred": (("antigravity-cli", "cache", "acp-auth-state.json"), ("antigravity-cli", "cache", "onboarding.json")),
       "env": {"AGY_CLI_FORCE_FILE_TOKEN_STORAGE": "1"},
