# ---------------------------------------------------------------- API keys
# An API key is pasted into Buzz (login.start with pays "key" gives the link to
# the page that makes one; login.finish takes the key). It is checked with one
# GET of the service's model list, with the key in a header only and redirects
# refused, kept in secrets/<harness>-key (mode 600) with which base and plan
# answered in secrets/<harness>-key.json, and given to the agent the way the
# pinned CLI reads a key: an environment variable, or the CLI's own file in a
# private home that holds nothing else. Nothing goes on a command line. The
# sign-in check and the model listing are the same GET.

# Each harness's key, as the pinned CLI reads it (checked on the Commerce Mac,
# 2026-11-16): service and the page that makes a key; the base URL(s) whose
# GET /models checks it; the header it goes in; `rejected` (status, body):
# what the service answers to a bad key; `env` (key, base): what the agent's
# environment gets; `home_env`: the private home for the slot (homes/<slot>),
# so the key agent never sees the subscription's files; `chat`: the models a
# person would pick from the service's list; `label` and `efforts` per model
# where known; and for Codex `install`, which puts the key where the CLI reads
# it (its own auth.json in that home, written by `codex login --with-api-key`
# on stdin: Codex's app-server does not read OPENAI_API_KEY from the environment).
